WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.348 --> 00:00:02.376
So who's my guest this week?

00:00:02.376 --> 00:00:06.292
The last Afghan Women's
Minister, Hasina Safi.

00:00:06.292 --> 00:00:10.956
Afghanistan, the 1970s,
an era of hope for women.

00:00:10.956 --> 00:00:13.823
As the '80s started, my guest turned 5,

00:00:13.823 --> 00:00:15.598
and everything changed.

00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:19.080
Over time, freedoms and
education were rolled back,

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.167
violence and humiliation commonplace.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:24.171
She and her family escaped,

00:00:24.171 --> 00:00:25.232
and as the years passed,

00:00:25.232 --> 00:00:26.993
she dedicated herself in exile

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:29.350
to campaigning for women's rights.

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:32.782
As democracy returned to
Afghanistan, so did she,

00:00:32.782 --> 00:00:35.846
eventually appointed to run
the Ministry of Women's Affairs

00:00:35.846 --> 00:00:37.913
under the last Afghan government,

00:00:37.913 --> 00:00:40.788
only to have to escape again last August,

00:00:40.788 --> 00:00:43.105
as the Taliban regained power.

00:00:43.105 --> 00:00:45.471
Ever since, she's been
living with her family

00:00:45.471 --> 00:00:48.952
as a refugee, in a London hotel.

00:00:48.952 --> 00:00:50.479
This interview is going to give you

00:00:50.479 --> 00:00:52.965
a remarkably powerful account

00:00:52.965 --> 00:00:55.733
of what it was like to flee the Taliban.

00:00:55.733 --> 00:00:56.760
Here's what's coming up.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.158
I had nothing to feel.

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:04.158
I was not even concerned
about what will happen to me,

00:01:04.411 --> 00:01:09.032
I was so concerned with the
big, big, big group of people

00:01:09.032 --> 00:01:10.927
that I was seeing there.

00:01:10.927 --> 00:01:15.383
What have we done that
we are facing this time?

00:01:15.383 --> 00:01:17.249
So it's very different.

00:01:17.249 --> 00:01:19.765
I really forgot that I am living.

00:01:19.765 --> 00:01:21.735
When I was eating, I was crying,

00:01:21.735 --> 00:01:24.345
because I thought that, "I'm eating,

00:01:24.345 --> 00:01:27.360
but there are many people
who are not eating there.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:28.777
Why should I eat?

00:01:30.305 --> 00:01:31.805
Why should I live?

00:01:33.202 --> 00:01:36.713
I couldn't help any women back there.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:52.669
Hasina, thank you so much for joining us.

00:01:52.669 --> 00:01:54.567
Welcome to the program.

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:56.795
Thank you very much for the opportunity.

00:01:56.795 --> 00:01:58.905
I wanted to start by saying,

00:01:58.905 --> 00:02:01.575
do you worry that the
world has forgotten a bit

00:02:01.575 --> 00:02:04.325
about Afghanistan, at the moment?

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:08.016
What I see today is

00:02:08.016 --> 00:02:11.516
there is a very total uncertainty globally

00:02:13.562 --> 00:02:15.657
about what to do,

00:02:15.657 --> 00:02:18.527
whereas the world has forgotten

00:02:18.527 --> 00:02:22.213
that there was a 20 years of investment

00:02:22.213 --> 00:02:25.663
on the human resources of Afghanistan,

00:02:25.663 --> 00:02:30.663
so there is always a hope and
an approach to move forward.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:35.236
They have forgotten, but
there are many opportunities

00:02:35.236 --> 00:02:40.236
if they just dig out about
or within their surroundings.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.657
How are the people that you're talking to,

00:02:42.657 --> 00:02:46.517
as you say, left alone under the Taliban?

00:02:46.517 --> 00:02:50.079
I think, basically, there
is still a lot of fear,

00:02:50.079 --> 00:02:52.896
there is a lot of uncertainty,

00:02:52.896 --> 00:02:55.479
there is a lot of hopelessness,

00:03:00.539 --> 00:03:03.027
and also insecurity.

00:03:03.027 --> 00:03:05.185
So the people really do not know,

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:09.102
because almost every
week, there is a new news,

00:03:10.562 --> 00:03:14.819
and instead of the
situation getting better,

00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:17.689
or the situation becoming hopeful,

00:03:17.689 --> 00:03:20.336
it's becoming deteriorating,

00:03:20.336 --> 00:03:22.758
starting from the day one,

00:03:22.758 --> 00:03:27.016
where stopping women for going to offices,

00:03:27.016 --> 00:03:29.941
abolishment of Women Ministry,

00:03:29.941 --> 00:03:34.238
the same thing, stopping
of women organizations,

00:03:34.238 --> 00:03:37.855
and asking the women who
were in leadership positions,

00:03:37.855 --> 00:03:39.974
those who were still in Afghanistan,

00:03:39.974 --> 00:03:41.962
to stay back home,

00:03:41.962 --> 00:03:43.890
and many other things.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:48.788
So day by day, there is
not a concrete or tangible

00:03:48.788 --> 00:03:51.254
indicator or directive

00:03:51.254 --> 00:03:52.416
through which you can see

00:03:52.416 --> 00:03:56.114
that there is a space or a place

00:03:56.114 --> 00:03:59.761
for the women of Afghanistan,
or for their future.

00:03:59.761 --> 00:04:01.834
But also, if I may say, with these reports

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:04.743
of girls getting ready
to go back into school,

00:04:04.743 --> 00:04:06.745
so excited, really looking forward

00:04:06.745 --> 00:04:08.215
to being able to go back in,

00:04:08.215 --> 00:04:11.194
the boys have been let back
in, the girls have not,

00:04:11.194 --> 00:04:14.531
but on the actual day they
were expected to go in,

00:04:14.531 --> 00:04:17.193
there is a U-turn, they
they don't let them in.

00:04:17.193 --> 00:04:19.483
Everyone is shocked. Why?

00:04:19.483 --> 00:04:22.974
Is it a sin to be a girl

00:04:22.974 --> 00:04:26.353
in a certain location?

00:04:26.353 --> 00:04:28.728
No, it's not. So what is it?

00:04:28.728 --> 00:04:31.177
It's a country, it's a structure.

00:04:31.177 --> 00:04:34.580
There are many, many big
things to think about.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:39.413
Why is a women's scarf, a
women's dress, a women's school,

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:42.192
why is this an agenda?

00:04:42.192 --> 00:04:46.914
There are many national
priorities to move forward

00:04:46.914 --> 00:04:50.258
for nation building, for the
development of the country.

00:04:50.258 --> 00:04:55.020
Why is this the first priority
at this critical situation?

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:56.239
And why do you think it is,

00:04:56.239 --> 00:04:57.953
knowing what you know of the Taliban,

00:04:57.953 --> 00:05:00.356
having lived through the
time that you've been in?

00:05:00.356 --> 00:05:02.608
I think there is no clear vision,

00:05:02.608 --> 00:05:04.745
there is no clear structure,

00:05:04.745 --> 00:05:07.348
there is no governance policy.

00:05:07.348 --> 00:05:10.271
There has been a big investment

00:05:10.271 --> 00:05:12.919
on the education of women,

00:05:12.919 --> 00:05:14.043
generally, education,

00:05:14.043 --> 00:05:16.055
and then specifically, on women and girls

00:05:16.055 --> 00:05:18.028
in the last 20 years,

00:05:18.028 --> 00:05:22.389
so for me, not only the
present de facto government

00:05:22.389 --> 00:05:25.323
but also the international community

00:05:25.323 --> 00:05:26.863
shall be accountable,

00:05:26.863 --> 00:05:29.577
because they have invested so much

00:05:29.577 --> 00:05:31.473
in education and health.

00:05:31.473 --> 00:05:33.268
Why are they just becoming

00:05:33.268 --> 00:05:36.653
only the people who are listening?

00:05:36.653 --> 00:05:38.661
Why there is no intervention?

00:05:38.661 --> 00:05:40.584
Where is the mutual accountability?

00:05:40.584 --> 00:05:42.695
Why are we not talking?

00:05:42.695 --> 00:05:47.695
We are all related to each
other as the basis of humanity,

00:05:47.966 --> 00:05:51.504
as the basis of investment
in the last 20 years.

00:05:51.504 --> 00:05:53.682
Do you think that women
will get an education,

00:05:53.682 --> 00:05:56.826
that women will be allowed
back into their jobs?

00:05:56.826 --> 00:06:01.070
What are your levels of
hope like at the moment?

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:04.814
Well, presently, from
the situation that I see

00:06:04.814 --> 00:06:07.506
about the present
structure in Afghanistan,

00:06:07.506 --> 00:06:09.347
I'm totally hopeless,

00:06:09.347 --> 00:06:13.935
because day after day, you hear things

00:06:13.935 --> 00:06:17.056
that you can't even imagine.

00:06:17.056 --> 00:06:20.589
Why would the girls not go to school,

00:06:20.589 --> 00:06:23.108
even if there is no resources?

00:06:23.108 --> 00:06:25.281
Where are the commitments? Why-

00:06:25.281 --> 00:06:26.457
For example we heard

00:06:26.457 --> 00:06:30.836
that the teachers and the
doctors are getting their pay,

00:06:30.836 --> 00:06:32.783
so why are they getting the pay

00:06:32.783 --> 00:06:35.083
if the children are not going to school?

00:06:35.083 --> 00:06:38.399
So there should be a
very clear definition,

00:06:38.399 --> 00:06:42.719
a very clear structure
of what they want to do.

00:06:42.719 --> 00:06:46.840
So that is why it is really hopeless

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.840
in present situation in Afghanistan.

00:06:50.749 --> 00:06:55.618
But on the whole, the world
is there to help each other.

00:06:55.618 --> 00:06:57.764
This is the time for the world

00:06:57.764 --> 00:07:00.568
to think about the people of Afghanistan,

00:07:00.568 --> 00:07:02.880
to think about the women of Afghanistan.

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.961
To take your mind back, if I may,

00:07:04.961 --> 00:07:07.334
to what happened in August.

00:07:07.334 --> 00:07:08.287
I mean, much has been made

00:07:08.287 --> 00:07:11.090
about how chaotic the evacuation was.

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:14.326
I think there was not a proper plan.

00:07:14.326 --> 00:07:18.805
There was not a proper plan
for the way it was proceeded.

00:07:18.805 --> 00:07:20.300
The decision was taken,

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:22.900
plans could be done,

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:24.501
plans could be made,

00:07:24.501 --> 00:07:27.723
discussions could be made
on an ad hoc, urgent basis,

00:07:27.723 --> 00:07:29.764
but they did not happen.

00:07:29.764 --> 00:07:32.523
That is why today, still,

00:07:32.523 --> 00:07:37.523
there are many, many people
who need to be evacuated,

00:07:37.531 --> 00:07:40.863
they are stuck, they
are back in Afghanistan,

00:07:40.863 --> 00:07:43.445
whose lives are real in danger.

00:07:43.445 --> 00:07:44.881
Because they helped the West
That is-

00:07:44.881 --> 00:07:47.530
and now they're on a list
with the Taliban, or-

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:49.232
Because they helped the West

00:07:49.232 --> 00:07:51.165
but they helped the humanity.
Yes.

00:07:51.165 --> 00:07:52.614
They wanted to live generally,

00:07:52.614 --> 00:07:53.447
But I mean, that's how
like-

00:07:53.447 --> 00:07:54.408
they would be viewed

00:07:54.408 --> 00:07:55.312
by the Taliban, potentially.

00:07:55.312 --> 00:07:56.145
That's why you say
Exactly.

00:07:56.145 --> 00:07:57.901
they would be in danger
Exactly.

00:07:57.901 --> 00:07:58.734
Exactly.

00:07:58.734 --> 00:08:01.366
So they are still stuck in Afghanistan.

00:08:01.366 --> 00:08:03.613
That is why, whenever I'm talking,

00:08:03.613 --> 00:08:07.170
I'm basically suggesting for the world

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:11.107
on three basic or fundamental issues.

00:08:11.107 --> 00:08:15.480
The first one is urgent
action on humanitarian

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:17.956
and protection of those people

00:08:17.956 --> 00:08:21.491
who really invested their lives forward

00:08:21.491 --> 00:08:25.885
for the success of the
international donation,

00:08:25.885 --> 00:08:27.631
or help, or support.

00:08:27.631 --> 00:08:32.564
The second thing is the midterm
solution for me, as a woman.

00:08:32.564 --> 00:08:36.558
The caretaker has no vision
for women, as a woman,

00:08:36.558 --> 00:08:38.483
and we can never ignore women,

00:08:38.483 --> 00:08:41.092
especially in a country like Afghanistan,

00:08:41.092 --> 00:08:44.768
where the majority of
population are women.

00:08:44.768 --> 00:08:47.886
And the third thing is the definition

00:08:47.886 --> 00:08:52.619
of the international
relation with Afghanistan.

00:08:52.619 --> 00:08:56.212
The international community
should really sit together

00:08:56.212 --> 00:09:00.104
and based on their priorities,

00:09:00.104 --> 00:09:04.768
they have to match up the
present situation of Afghanistan

00:09:04.768 --> 00:09:07.233
for a reason, which is help and support

00:09:07.233 --> 00:09:09.483
the humanity, the people, and the women

00:09:09.483 --> 00:09:11.082
of Afghanistan.
Beyond financial aid.

00:09:11.082 --> 00:09:12.138
Exactly.
you're talking about,

00:09:12.138 --> 00:09:14.380
because, of course, that has been the way

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:16.743
that Afghanistan has just
about avoided famine,

00:09:16.743 --> 00:09:20.311
because of the levels of donation,
food, aid, on that front,

00:09:20.311 --> 00:09:22.851
but you're talking about
actually intervening.

00:09:22.851 --> 00:09:23.985
Exactly.

00:09:23.985 --> 00:09:26.485
How did you actually escape?

00:09:28.207 --> 00:09:31.176
Emma, to be honest, I
was not planning to leave

00:09:31.176 --> 00:09:32.777
Really?
Yes.

00:09:32.777 --> 00:09:34.790
My plan was that I cannot leave

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:38.185
because there are so many
women who need me here.

00:09:38.185 --> 00:09:42.645
But after that, I saw that the
situation was deteriorating,

00:09:42.645 --> 00:09:44.741
and some of my close friends suggested

00:09:44.741 --> 00:09:48.081
that, "Your life is valuable for us."

00:09:48.081 --> 00:09:53.081
I had worked a lot with
the British organizations

00:09:53.243 --> 00:09:54.910
in Foreign Ministry,

00:09:55.902 --> 00:10:00.369
and I really don't know
how I wrote the email.

00:10:00.369 --> 00:10:02.330
I did not know who to contact,

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:06.335
but I wrote the email in
the contacts which I had,

00:10:06.335 --> 00:10:11.335
and then, I think, after two days,

00:10:11.335 --> 00:10:16.335
and definitely coordination
of the international sisters

00:10:16.728 --> 00:10:21.728
who had made an informal group
to save the lives of women,

00:10:22.381 --> 00:10:26.582
especially the women who were
in decision-making positions,

00:10:26.582 --> 00:10:28.835
they were in constant contact.

00:10:28.835 --> 00:10:29.668
They were telling me,

00:10:29.668 --> 00:10:31.534
"You will get an email,
you will get an email."

00:10:31.534 --> 00:10:33.692
And almost every second, they would say,

00:10:33.692 --> 00:10:36.428
"Did you get an email?
Did you get a email?"

00:10:36.428 --> 00:10:40.303
And then after, when I
received the email from them

00:10:40.303 --> 00:10:45.294
that, "You have to come to
Baron Hotel in 12 hours."

00:10:46.589 --> 00:10:48.896
I did not know where Baron Hotel was.

00:10:48.896 --> 00:10:51.859
That's in Afghanistan? Yes.
Yes, yes.

00:10:51.859 --> 00:10:56.192
I did not have any vehicle,
so I messaged them back,

00:10:57.071 --> 00:10:59.699
not the email address,

00:10:59.699 --> 00:11:02.224
but the group of women
who were helping me,

00:11:02.224 --> 00:11:06.104
I told them, "I have no
vehicles, nothing to go,

00:11:06.104 --> 00:11:09.057
so can you arrange for the vehicles?"

00:11:09.057 --> 00:11:10.971
They told me, "We will try."

00:11:10.971 --> 00:11:12.206
So they arranged once,

00:11:12.206 --> 00:11:14.572
and then I think there
were some security issues,

00:11:14.572 --> 00:11:15.934
they canceled it.

00:11:15.934 --> 00:11:19.998
Because, like, I never was
assuming this situation,

00:11:19.998 --> 00:11:21.669
so that is why.

00:11:21.669 --> 00:11:24.264
And I was a role model to many people

00:11:24.264 --> 00:11:28.336
because I also believe in a balanced life,

00:11:28.336 --> 00:11:31.493
so I was a lot in
public, everyone knew me,

00:11:31.493 --> 00:11:33.824
shopkeepers, everyone knew me there.

00:11:33.824 --> 00:11:37.007
That is why there was a
lot of security issues

00:11:37.007 --> 00:11:38.422
on those days.

00:11:38.422 --> 00:11:42.360
One of the other female
minister, former minister,

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:47.360
she called me and she gave me
the number who had helped her,

00:11:47.467 --> 00:11:52.050
and they were demanding for
some financial, like, rent,

00:11:52.984 --> 00:11:55.767
so I got my son's piggy bank,

00:11:55.767 --> 00:11:58.884
where we were, all the
time, in his birthday,

00:11:58.884 --> 00:11:59.724
we were giving him,

00:11:59.724 --> 00:12:03.146
and we broke that, and we had some money

00:12:03.146 --> 00:12:07.264
which we could give the logistic company,

00:12:07.264 --> 00:12:09.142
or the people who-

00:12:09.142 --> 00:12:11.406
We did not go through the formal airport

00:12:11.406 --> 00:12:13.464
because it was too crowded.

00:12:13.464 --> 00:12:16.894
Someone told us that
you can go from behind,

00:12:16.894 --> 00:12:19.303
the drivers, they guided us.

00:12:19.303 --> 00:12:22.470
We went there. The family was with me.

00:12:23.816 --> 00:12:25.163
They told me to go in,

00:12:25.163 --> 00:12:28.467
but when I went there, it
was a terrible situation.

00:12:28.467 --> 00:12:30.283
There was a lot of fire guns,

00:12:30.283 --> 00:12:34.470
there was a lot of lashing,
they were lashing people.

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:36.951
Some of the family got lashes.

00:12:36.951 --> 00:12:40.307
The Taliban were doing this?
Yes, yes, yes.

00:12:40.307 --> 00:12:42.840
And some of your family
Yes.

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:45.459
Three of the family members
received lashes?

00:12:45.459 --> 00:12:46.858
received lashes.

00:12:46.858 --> 00:12:49.130
And then I decided that, no way,

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:51.188
because they were also gun firing,

00:12:51.188 --> 00:12:55.541
and I said if something
happens to them and I'm alive,

00:12:55.541 --> 00:13:00.091
I will never live with that guilt.

00:13:00.091 --> 00:13:02.327
So we decided, me and my husband,

00:13:02.327 --> 00:13:04.494
that we will go back home,

00:13:05.345 --> 00:13:07.325
whatever happened on the way.

00:13:07.325 --> 00:13:08.816
I was on half of the way

00:13:08.816 --> 00:13:12.203
when my friend, the former minister,

00:13:12.203 --> 00:13:15.032
she called me, and she
scolded me, in fact.

00:13:15.032 --> 00:13:17.784
She said, "Don't do this mistake.

00:13:17.784 --> 00:13:18.651
You have to come."

00:13:18.651 --> 00:13:22.684
There is a canal

00:13:22.684 --> 00:13:26.537
where the suicide attack
happened two days after,

00:13:26.537 --> 00:13:28.639
so she said, "We also came from that way."

00:13:28.639 --> 00:13:32.539
I said I cannot go because
my family is with me

00:13:32.539 --> 00:13:36.281
and I had a elderly, sick mother.

00:13:36.281 --> 00:13:39.410
She said, "No, whatever
you do, if you go back,

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:42.350
I know you will not be alive."

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:45.814
And then, when I went
there, there was a big crowd

00:13:45.814 --> 00:13:48.503
going up, going down, going up.

00:13:48.503 --> 00:13:52.253
I think maybe 1,000 or
800 people were there.

00:13:53.724 --> 00:13:54.891
So we came up.

00:13:56.173 --> 00:14:00.925
Finally, we came, and I called a number.

00:14:00.925 --> 00:14:04.671
I don't know, it's maybe
destiny, or God helped us,

00:14:04.671 --> 00:14:06.388
the number went through,

00:14:06.388 --> 00:14:10.326
and it was one of my female friends

00:14:10.326 --> 00:14:11.605
who were organizing this,

00:14:11.605 --> 00:14:14.879
and I called her, and I said,
"I don't know what to do.

00:14:14.879 --> 00:14:16.520
I'm in here, in the crowd.

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:21.029
I'm on the top of that
dirty ditch with the family.

00:14:21.029 --> 00:14:21.897
What to do?"

00:14:21.897 --> 00:14:23.621
So you're standing with
all of your family,

00:14:23.621 --> 00:14:24.852
there's a lot of people around.

00:14:24.852 --> 00:14:25.685
Almost-
I'm just trying

00:14:25.685 --> 00:14:26.568
to picture this.
Yes.

00:14:26.568 --> 00:14:29.110
And you're at the top
of a ditch, you said,

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:31.628
Yes, yes, there is-
and you're ringing someone

00:14:31.628 --> 00:14:33.036
to try and find out
Yes, yes.

00:14:33.036 --> 00:14:34.644
how you can leave Afghanistan,

00:14:34.644 --> 00:14:36.487
how you can escape.
Yes, yes.

00:14:36.487 --> 00:14:38.305
How are you feeling at this time,

00:14:38.305 --> 00:14:40.355
that you've got elderly family with you,

00:14:40.355 --> 00:14:41.999
you've got your children, and you-

00:14:41.999 --> 00:14:43.779
That's why, Emma, I told you

00:14:43.779 --> 00:14:46.446
that I really did not understand

00:14:49.124 --> 00:14:54.124
what was all the struggle that
I did in the last 20 years?

00:14:54.606 --> 00:14:58.286
It was the second time that
I had to leave my country.

00:14:58.286 --> 00:15:02.013
I left my country when I was 5 years old,

00:15:02.013 --> 00:15:05.597
when Russia invaded Afghanistan,

00:15:05.597 --> 00:15:10.597
and from 5 years old till 25,

00:15:11.292 --> 00:15:14.481
I struggled with each drop of my blood

00:15:14.481 --> 00:15:19.331
to go back, invest my
knowledge, invest my talent,

00:15:20.664 --> 00:15:25.318
for my coming generations,
so that they do not feel.

00:15:25.318 --> 00:15:28.712
And I really was killed
on that night, Emma.

00:15:28.712 --> 00:15:31.018
I had nothing to feel.

00:15:31.018 --> 00:15:32.899
I had no feelings.

00:15:32.899 --> 00:15:34.009
My only concern,

00:15:34.009 --> 00:15:39.009
I was not even concerned
about what will happen to me,

00:15:39.271 --> 00:15:44.262
I was so concerned with the
big, big, big group of people

00:15:44.262 --> 00:15:46.051
that I was seeing there.

00:15:46.051 --> 00:15:48.406
People were sitting with their papers,

00:15:48.406 --> 00:15:51.187
passports, everything,

00:15:51.187 --> 00:15:52.953
and they were saying, "Oh,
I have worked with this.

00:15:52.953 --> 00:15:54.305
Oh, I have..."

00:15:54.305 --> 00:15:57.388
And I was like, "How helpless we are.

00:16:00.475 --> 00:16:05.475
What have we done that
we are facing this time?"

00:16:05.869 --> 00:16:08.786
So that is why it was really, like,

00:16:10.311 --> 00:16:14.232
to be very honest, I could not
feel anything till one month.

00:16:14.232 --> 00:16:16.226
I was all the time crying.

00:16:16.226 --> 00:16:20.399
In the middle of the night, I
was sweating, I was waking up,

00:16:20.399 --> 00:16:22.798
and I was thinking someone
is knocking the door,

00:16:22.798 --> 00:16:25.786
or there is something happening outside.

00:16:25.786 --> 00:16:29.107
There are some of their own voices,

00:16:29.107 --> 00:16:31.430
or whatever they were doing.

00:16:31.430 --> 00:16:35.147
So it's very different, very different.

00:16:35.147 --> 00:16:37.681
I really forgot that I am living.

00:16:37.681 --> 00:16:39.731
When I was eating, I was crying,

00:16:39.731 --> 00:16:42.304
because I thought that, "I'm eating,

00:16:42.304 --> 00:16:45.308
but there are many people
who are not eating there.

00:16:45.308 --> 00:16:46.725
Why should I eat?

00:16:48.235 --> 00:16:49.735
Why should I live?

00:16:51.215 --> 00:16:55.501
I couldn't help any women back there.

00:16:55.501 --> 00:16:56.751
I'm so sorry.

00:16:57.984 --> 00:16:59.901
Still it's like that.

00:17:03.522 --> 00:17:06.522
It's difficult. It's very difficult.

00:17:07.533 --> 00:17:09.578
I think even just that
moment that you described,

00:17:09.578 --> 00:17:11.170
where you have to be with your family

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:15.137
and you've got to think
about them and being safe,

00:17:15.137 --> 00:17:20.137
but you have such a duty to
your people and to your country.

00:17:21.194 --> 00:17:26.194
Even then, I tried to
help, but I was helpless.

00:17:26.284 --> 00:17:28.778
I couldn't help myself,

00:17:28.778 --> 00:17:31.107
I couldn't help anyone.

00:17:31.107 --> 00:17:34.709
So it's very difficult.

00:17:34.709 --> 00:17:36.589
And then after that,

00:17:36.589 --> 00:17:39.460
the soldier told us, "You are safe now,"

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:42.877
and then they took us inside the airport,

00:17:46.678 --> 00:17:48.661
because we left that place,

00:17:48.661 --> 00:17:51.285
so he did not know where to take us,

00:17:51.285 --> 00:17:53.943
so I showed the paper, and then he took us

00:17:53.943 --> 00:17:58.885
to that ground where the
planes were departing.

00:17:58.885 --> 00:18:02.201
They were sitting and departing.

00:18:02.201 --> 00:18:06.554
I think maybe for three or
five hours, we were there.

00:18:06.554 --> 00:18:10.804
There were the big space
planes, they were leaving.

00:18:12.682 --> 00:18:17.582
All of a sudden, I saw that
it was written 'Royal Space'

00:18:19.278 --> 00:18:21.580
and I told the soldier that,

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:26.580
"Can you show this paper
to that commander?"

00:18:27.195 --> 00:18:28.946
He said, "I'm not allowed to."

00:18:28.946 --> 00:18:31.783
I said, "Okay, if you're not allowed,

00:18:31.783 --> 00:18:35.077
I will stay here, no problem."

00:18:35.077 --> 00:18:37.682
I have been constantly asking him

00:18:37.682 --> 00:18:39.329
about how long should we stay?

00:18:39.329 --> 00:18:41.786
He said, "We don't know."

00:18:41.786 --> 00:18:46.786
And then I think it was around
one o'clock, at 1:00 a.m.,

00:18:47.071 --> 00:18:51.696
that the soldier went, but he came back.

00:18:51.696 --> 00:18:53.546
He said, "I will take the paper."

00:18:53.546 --> 00:18:58.546
So he took the paper to the UK soldier,

00:18:58.642 --> 00:19:00.776
commander, I think,

00:19:00.776 --> 00:19:02.912
then he took the paper, he read that,

00:19:02.912 --> 00:19:05.155
and he took that to inside the plane.

00:19:05.155 --> 00:19:07.020
Maybe there or somewhere,

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:09.439
and then they waved to us,

00:19:09.439 --> 00:19:13.289
and after that, we entered the bus,

00:19:13.289 --> 00:19:16.877
and they said that, "You
are in safe hands now."

00:19:16.877 --> 00:19:20.339
And we were all crying Emma on that time.

00:19:20.339 --> 00:19:21.588
We even didn't know

00:19:21.588 --> 00:19:23.421
how to hug each other.

00:19:24.988 --> 00:19:27.951
So it was a difficult time.

00:19:27.951 --> 00:19:31.520
And then after that,
we came to the UK base,

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:34.172
and from that onwards,

00:19:34.172 --> 00:19:39.172
I think, as a human being,
I have to recognize that,

00:19:39.833 --> 00:19:44.793
that it was all care and
humanity for everyone.

00:19:44.793 --> 00:19:49.793
There was no special, there
was no prioritization,

00:19:50.451 --> 00:19:52.770
but they were just treating everyone.

00:19:52.770 --> 00:19:56.359
I know how hard and difficult
it must be for them.

00:19:56.359 --> 00:19:59.438
They have been in
constant work as a person.

00:19:59.438 --> 00:20:01.747
You're still with your
family, as I understand it,

00:20:01.747 --> 00:20:02.941
in a hotel,
Yes.

00:20:02.941 --> 00:20:04.090
In the UK.
Yes.

00:20:04.090 --> 00:20:06.164
And it's about seven months or so now

00:20:06.164 --> 00:20:09.360
that you will have been
in this accommodation.

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:10.907
How has that been?

00:20:10.907 --> 00:20:12.007
You know, we're thinking a lot

00:20:12.007 --> 00:20:14.786
about how many people are
displaced at the moment

00:20:14.786 --> 00:20:16.183
around the world.

00:20:16.183 --> 00:20:18.111
This is the second time
that you've done this,

00:20:18.111 --> 00:20:20.682
but how has it been
for your family and you

00:20:20.682 --> 00:20:23.110
living in the hotel?

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:26.839
Actually, to be very honest, Emma,

00:20:26.839 --> 00:20:30.033
they were very concerned about my life,

00:20:30.033 --> 00:20:33.653
so none of them have
been telling me anything,

00:20:33.653 --> 00:20:38.172
but from what I see, they
are hiding their feelings

00:20:38.172 --> 00:20:40.382
because of me, because they know

00:20:40.382 --> 00:20:44.715
that I'm very, very concerned
about the people back there.

00:20:44.715 --> 00:20:45.978
When you say that, you mean your family?

00:20:45.978 --> 00:20:48.809
Yes. I know it's difficult for them.

00:20:48.809 --> 00:20:52.379
It's very difficult,
because a home is a home,

00:20:52.379 --> 00:20:54.296
and a hotel is a hotel.

00:20:55.857 --> 00:20:57.489
We are getting everything.

00:20:57.489 --> 00:21:00.740
There is food, there is
rooms, there is internet.

00:21:00.740 --> 00:21:03.251
But definitely, if it's home,

00:21:03.251 --> 00:21:06.351
all the time, we say it's home sweet home,

00:21:06.351 --> 00:21:08.565
so home is always sweet,

00:21:08.565 --> 00:21:11.759
but they haven't been
saying anything about that,

00:21:11.759 --> 00:21:14.252
because whenever they-

00:21:14.252 --> 00:21:18.253
How I understand that they are concerned

00:21:18.253 --> 00:21:20.753
is whenever they say this, they say,

00:21:20.753 --> 00:21:22.538
"Oh, we are blessed that you are alive."

00:21:22.538 --> 00:21:25.283
So that is what, on that time,

00:21:25.283 --> 00:21:28.738
I analyze that they must be missing home,

00:21:28.738 --> 00:21:31.385
they must be missing their home,

00:21:31.385 --> 00:21:34.326
they must be missing home here.

00:21:34.326 --> 00:21:38.248
Do you think you can
build a life in the UK?

00:21:38.248 --> 00:21:43.115
Of course I can, because
I believe in humanity,

00:21:43.115 --> 00:21:47.673
and the reason that today I'm here

00:21:47.673 --> 00:21:52.673
is basically the human belief that I have,

00:21:52.821 --> 00:21:57.795
and that is why I again
stress on humanity,

00:21:57.795 --> 00:22:02.281
on connection, on relation, on confidence,

00:22:02.281 --> 00:22:04.438
because it's nothing else

00:22:04.438 --> 00:22:08.822
but the high value of those friends

00:22:08.822 --> 00:22:12.541
who really believed and
worked with me as a human.

00:22:12.541 --> 00:22:15.061
I did not ask them, really.

00:22:15.061 --> 00:22:16.744
They asked me at the beginning,

00:22:16.744 --> 00:22:18.377
"Hasina, how are you?

00:22:18.377 --> 00:22:20.043
Hasina, are you fine?

00:22:20.043 --> 00:22:21.730
Hasina, are you okay?

00:22:21.730 --> 00:22:23.751
Hasina, good morning. How are you?

00:22:23.751 --> 00:22:25.590
Did you eat? Did you-"

00:22:25.590 --> 00:22:28.408
So there is no policy or anything in here.

00:22:28.408 --> 00:22:31.775
It's just a real connection of humanity.

00:22:31.775 --> 00:22:35.432
I'm very confident that I can do that.

00:22:35.432 --> 00:22:39.029
Do you think you'll ever
be able to go back again

00:22:39.029 --> 00:22:40.454
and live in Afghanistan?

00:22:40.454 --> 00:22:41.832
Yes.
You do?

00:22:41.832 --> 00:22:45.700
Yes, because I'm a very hopeful person.

00:22:45.700 --> 00:22:47.687
I'm a very positive person.

00:22:47.687 --> 00:22:49.065
I will have challenges,

00:22:49.065 --> 00:22:50.799
we will have challenges,

00:22:50.799 --> 00:22:54.147
but I know that struggle brings result,

00:22:54.147 --> 00:22:58.166
and I will struggle to bring
the result, so that is why.

00:22:58.166 --> 00:23:02.379
I am hopeful, but I need to
struggle double and triple

00:23:02.379 --> 00:23:05.296
to really get to those who need me.

00:23:06.317 --> 00:23:09.380
Hasina Safi, thank you so
much for talking to me.

00:23:09.380 --> 00:23:10.900
Thank you very much.

00:23:10.900 --> 00:23:13.420
And thank you to you for being with us,

00:23:13.420 --> 00:23:16.375
and listening to that
remarkable conversation.

00:23:16.375 --> 00:23:19.567
Until we meet again, do
take care, and goodbye.

